  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Friday)\nIssued at 1102 PM CDT Fri Oct 9 2026\n\nThe upper ridging is expected to strengthen over the southeast\nMonday into the middle of next week. The sunny skies and building\nupper level winds will make for a very warm conditions with highs\nclimbing back into the mid to upper 80s and lows in the lower \n60s.\n\nAn upper level low and associated longwave trough axis makes some\nslight progress pushing east into the upper ridge over the area \ntowards the end of the week/weekend. However, over much of the \narea the surface and upper ridge remain stout. However, enough \nforcing aloft and moisture convergence does setup over much of \nTennessee to produce some precipitation over that area. Our \nsouthern middle Tennessee counties could see some low end \nprecipitation chances, but consistency is too low to include at \nthis time. Most guidance does push a dry cold front through the \narea Friday or Friday night. This will bring cooler weather to to \nthe area that is more seasonable into the weekend.",
